; flush of a file that is not open for writing is a runtime error (Free
; Pascal's errors 103 and 105).
; RUN: %p3 --mode=tp %S/Inputs/flush/errors.pas -o %t
; RUN: not %t closed %t.tmp 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=CLOSED %s
; CLOSED: Runtime error: 'flush' of a file that is not open (file '{{.*}}.tmp')
; RUN: not %t reading %t.tmp 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=READING %s
; READING: Runtime error: 'flush' of a file that is not open for writing (file '{{.*}}.tmp')
; RUN: not %t input %t.tmp 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=INPUT %s
; INPUT: Runtime error: 'flush' of a file that is not open for writing (file 'input')
; RUN: %t ok %t.tmp | FileCheck --check-prefix=OK %s
; OK: fine
